### 4. Login certo → 200 + token (salva o token numa variável)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hemerson@teste.com",
  "senha": "senhaForte123"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 5. Senha errada → 401
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hemerson@teste.com",
  "senha": "senhaErrada999"
}

### 6. E-mail que não existe → 401 com a MESMA mensagem
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ninguem@teste.com",
  "senha": "senhaForte123"
}

### 7. /me sem token → 401
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me

### 8. /me com token → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Token adulterado → 401
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x